.th CHDIR I 5/15/74
.sh NAME
chdir \*- change working directory
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd chdir
directory
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Directory
becomes the new working directory.
The process must have execute (search)
permission in
.it directory.
.s3
Because a new process is created to execute each command,
.it chdir
would be ineffective if it were written as a
normal command.
If possible therefore
it is recognized and executed
by the Shell.
If necessary, the Shell invokes "/etc/glob" ( which in turn invokes
"/etc/chdir" ) to interpret the normal pattern matching symbols.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
sh (I), pwd (I), glob (VIII), chdir (VIII)
.sh BUGS
